# Vocabulary versions implemented in this repo.
# Compare against spec/VOCAB_VERSIONS to detect drift.
# Run scripts/check-downstream-versions.sh from spec/ to check all repos at once.
# Update this file when the system prompt or agent capabilities reflect new vocabulary.
# core 3.3 (2026-06-16): added cascade:AIAsserted (ungrounded general-purpose-AI
#   provenance leaf), cascade:ProxyAgent (caregiver-proxy actor + actsForPatient/
#   proxyRelationship/proxyGrantedAt/etc.); plus cascade:AIGenerationActivity,
#   cascade:AdvisoryApplicationActivity, cascade:GenerationTrigger (from v3.1/3.2).
# clinical 1.9 (2026-06-17): shapes-only — cascade:AIExtracted is now a valid
#   cascade:dataProvenance value on clinical records.
# 2026-07-15 batched draft sync: taught the system prompt the notes/ oa:Annotation
#   container (workbench v1-draft.0.5), the evidence facet model (evidence v1-draft.0.2),
#   and workbench:userSourceLabel (v1-draft.0.4). Per D-PATH, drafts stay unrowed until
#   v1.0 graduation; no version row change.
# core 3.4 (2026-08-03): the pod export manifest is now describable vocabulary, so the
#   prompt teaches reading manifest.ttl as a first orienting call instead of only parsing
#   it: cascade:ExportManifest (a dcat:Dataset), cascade:RecordSummary (a void:Dataset
#   whose per-domain counts are rdfs:subPropertyOf void:entities) and the seven count
#   properties, cascade:InteractionScenario (+ involvedResources / severity /
#   requiresCrossProvenance), and cascade:provenanceLayers. Also teaches that the five
#   *Days properties count DAYS COVERED and must never be reported as record counts, and
#   adds the reading-level terms cascade:date (with the health:date second spelling),
#   cascade:sampleCount and cascade:loincCode.
# health 2.5 (2026-08-03): the five clinical record classes (health:LabResultRecord,
#   ConditionRecord, AllergyRecord, ImmunizationRecord, FamilyHistoryRecord) are now
#   defined and shaped, and the six wellness containers (health:ActivityData, SleepData,
#   HeartRateData, BloodPressureData, HRVData, BodyMeasurements) are rdfs:subClassOf
#   health:HealthProfile, so the prompt now says the history properties hang off those six
#   subjects. Also teaches the namespace-boundary rule: health: vs clinical: is historical,
#   not a provenance signal — cascade:dataProvenance is the only source-of-truth for origin.
# clinical 1.13 (2026-08-03): clinical:LabResult / Condition / Allergy / Immunization are
#   deprecated in favour of their health: equivalents but are NOT removed, no emitter
#   changed, and existing pods hold both. The prompt gains a dedicated "Two Spellings"
#   section teaching that both must be queried, with the per-concept predicate table (the
#   two spellings share no predicates), and every clinical jq example in the prompt now
#   reads both. Also teaches the v1.10-v1.12 graph edges clinical:hasEncounter,
#   clinical:indicationReference (traverse the superproperty to get both stated and
#   clinical:parsedIndicationReference edges, and present them differently) and
#   clinical:linkedCondition superseding the untraversable clinical:linkedConditionIds
#   literal, plus the new ConsultationNote shape and the two unenforced value sets.
# health 2.6 / clinical 1.14 / coverage 1.4 / checkup 3.3 (2026-08-08): shapes-only
#   alignment to ratified standards (spec PR the-cascade-protocol/spec#16). The system
#   prompt is taught the four facts that change what the agent may ASSUME when reading a
#   pod: lab interpretation is the HL7 v3 ObservationInterpretation code system (and
#   "unknown" means the source carried none, not "normal"); labCategory, testCode,
#   icd10Code and snomedCode are repeatable, so a dual-coded problem is one condition and
#   not two; source-carried dates may be xsd:date, and a date with no time means the time
#   was not recorded; clinical:Encounter is now validated at all, and coverage:coverageType
#   is no longer a closed enum. checkup 3.3 is an ICD-10-CM pattern fix with no agent-facing
#   consequence and is recorded here only to keep the rows in step.
core=3.4
health=2.6
clinical=1.14
coverage=1.4
checkup=3.3
pots=1.4
